@startuml 07-voice-session-and-finish
title Sequence 07 - Voice session activation and interview finish
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Candidate
participant "Candidate page" as P
participant "HTTP delivery" as H
participant "Runtime coordinator" as R
participant "Execution Lifecycle" as L
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "GPT-Live driver" as D
participant "GPT-Live" as G

== Request session attempt (intent = activate) ==
Candidate -> P : start voice
P -> P : create WebRTC offer (SDP)
P -> H : POST /candidate/executions/{id}/session-attempts\n{sdp, intent, expectedVersion, controllerId, idempotencyKey}
H -> H : cookie, origin, CSRF, assignment and controller checks
H -> R : Attempt
alt same key and same intent already succeeded
  R --> H : original answer replayed
  H --> P : 200 original attempt and SDP answer
else new
  R -> L : open attempt (2 x 30 s within 90 s)
  R -> DB : read pinned revision, build progress
  R -> DB : joined tx: attempt authority, pending command,\ncoverage and session shell
  R -> D : create session (instructions without salary ceiling)
  D -> G : create session, SDP exchange
  G --> D : session id, SDP answer
  D -> G : attach sideband
  R -> DB : fenced tx: retain provider session id,\nstore original answer for replay
  H --> P : 201 {attemptId, sessionId, sdp, executionVersion, sessionCondition}
end
P -> G : apply SDP answer, media flows over WebRTC

== Ready ==
P -> H : POST .../session-attempts/{attempt_id}/ready {controllerId, expectedVersion}
H -> R : Ready
R -> L : is this the current attempt?
R -> DB : record browser readiness
H --> P : 200 {sessionCondition ready | pending}
note right : readiness never marks a question asked,\nheard or answered. A stale attempt gets 409 IRT_NOT_READY.
note over L : lifecycle moves the execution to RUNNING on successful activation

== Finish with "Selesai" (BR-CORE-070) ==
Candidate -> P : press Selesai and confirm
P -> H : POST /candidate/executions/{id}/complete {expectedVersion}
H -> R : CompleteInterview
R -> DB : seal remaining stages in order (handoffs)
R -> DB : close local session records
R -> L : Complete(progress id)
L -> DB : commit COMPLETED
R -> D : close provider session by stored id
D -> G : session.close
note right : best effort. A provider failure never\nundoes the completion
H --> P : 200 execution COMPLETED  (repeat returns the same 200)
P -> P : release microphone, show COMPLETED

note over R, DB : in progress (T21): the model ending the interview\nitself through a complete_stage tool is not built
@enduml
